# Plugin is a something that exposes or enhances your basic software.
# So when we write the provider plugin it will download the same plugin, like aws- aws plugin, gcp - google plugin, azue - azure plugin.

# ......tf               -- the terraform will read all the .tf files in the current directory.

# we can write all the terraform script in a single file.

# All the terraform folder will be downloaded in the .terraform folder.

# la -al                 -- all the plugins will be saved.
# Terraform init         -- used to download the requied plugin to local teeraform server and then terraform uses these plugins to connect/login & create resources on cloud environments.
# Terraform plan         -- used for Dry Run and reads all the terraform scripts in local serve inside the directory where terraform command is executed.
# Terraform apply        -- execute and apply the changes where terraform reads all the scripts in local server inside the directory where terraform command is executed.
                             created the resources on cloud and once the resources are created.
                             terraform creates a file called terraoform.tf state file on local server about all the resources it created with apply.
# Terraform destroy      -- reads all the local terraform.tf state files in the current directory where terraform command we run and deletes all the resources.
# Terraform Registry     -- AWS -- Documentation -- Check for Argument Reference.

-----------------Single Instance with Tags-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------      

#  ec2.tf                                   -- Assign the Tags.
= resource "aws_instance" "web-server" 
{
ami = "ami-0c24c764e44ed98f2"
tags = {
  Name = "terra_user"
  env = "dev"                            -- Tags 
  a = "b"                                -- Tags
}
instance_type = "t3.micro"
count = 2
key_name = "key"
security_group = "launch-wizard-3"
}

